\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Milla Jovovich brought stony-faced supermodel moxie to 2002's underrated first film and her subsequent franchise was a mixed bag. But there's a whole global fandom of obsessives who feel that none of these movies truly got the crux of what made Capcom's original games such an all-night fixation. One of those people turns out to be filmmaker Zach Cregger, who, between "Barbarian" and his Oscar-winning "Weapons," can now write his own ticket. As unlikely as it seems, this reboot is a project he has spent a considerable amount of his newfound Hollywood capital pursuing and you have to love him for it. Apocalyptic Raccoon City and a viral zombie outbreak are sure to figure, but also, given the Cregger of it all, spooky subterranean passages and confident performances, this time from Austin Abrams and Paul Walter Hauser. -- Joshua Rothkopf}
